  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "If \\(y\\) varies directly as \\(x,\\) and if \\(y=8\\) when \\(x=4,\\) the value of \\(y\\) when \\(x=-8\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-16\\)",
    "B": "\\(-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2\\)",
    "D": "\\(4k,\\) \\(k=\\pm1,\\) \\(\\pm2,\\) \\(\\ldots\\)",
    "E": "\\(16k,\\) \\(k=\\pm1,\\) \\(\\pm2,\\) \\(\\ldots\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Direct variation means \\(y=kx\\) for a fixed nonzero constant \\(k\\). Using \\(y=8\\) when \\(x=4\\),\n\\[\n8=4k,\\qquad k=2.\n\\]\nThus \\(y=2x\\), and when \\(x=-8\\),\n\\[\ny=2(-8)=-16.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{-16}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
